-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Fantasy World Dizzy
  Publisher   Code Masters, 1989
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Dizzy 3 - Fantasy World Dizzy (1989)(Code
              Masters)(128K)[a2][a2].z80
  MD5         2f84d85c52046a8b7a2ec6f2ebd415bc

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original (+0.00% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless, the plain
              .nex as control, input keyed to the game loop update 0xA711,
              lockstep checked at every update (equal in all 30 trials), SPACE
              tapped in boxes and the title by the game's own input poll)

  Changes     1.0: Dean Woodyatt's Fantasy World Dizzy build moved to the 128K
              release (AY music), his plot hook at 28 MHz, whole alt ROM
              image, loading screen

  Note        The 128K release, so the AY music plays. Dean Woodyatt's Fantasy
              World Dizzy build: Dizzy is four hardware sprites, so he no
              longer takes the colours of the scenery he walks through; his
              plot hook now runs at 28 MHz. Loading screen from the tape.
              Known issues: when Dizzy stands in the animated fire, his sprite
              can be a frame out of step with the fire drawn under him (3
              frames in 300; he stays whole). Missing: no Enhanced colour set
              (rated easy: Dizzy's frames match Treasure Island Dizzy's
              Spec256 colours); five immunity cheats checked only at their
              code, as their rooms were not reached; only the dungeon and the
              first rooms checked in testing; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immune to flame
   3  Immune to rat
   4  Immune to dragon's fire
   5  Immune to armorog
   6  Immune to gator
   7  Immune to sharp daggers

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

