-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by the owner in JNext 2026-11-05: approved

  Replay      3 recordings of the 128K release IDENTICAL on rework v128 (bot
              walks of 12,010 / 12,007 / 12,004 frames: the dungeon, the
              troll's dialogue, deaths in the fire, a game over and restart,
              the inventory, the Smuggler's Hideout): 5,983 plots pixel-
              perfect, 5,935 erases, 12,122 ISR hide checks (104 on the hide
              path), 100 room wipes and 96 boxes hiding Dizzy, equal to the
              original's; the game never touches the tail and latch in the
              printer buffer nor the alt ROM hook bytes; 4 negative controls
              detected; clock matrix 5 hook sites x 4 incoming clocks = 20
              cases PASS, a forced 3.5 MHz exit detected; ROM paths: every ROM
              byte as recorded; start-up tail never read before written

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: loading screen, title, play reached,
              frames viewed, also with a cheat on; AY music written (550 data
              writes a second in play, as the original); flicker 300 frames: 3
              out of step (Dizzy standing in the animated fire, which redraws
              under his sprite on its own cycle; frames viewed, Dizzy whole),
              0 vanished, 0 transients, one-frame attribute blinks as the
              original; 15-minute soak against the original .z80: no freeze,
              loop or crash; no person played it

  Coverage    the dungeon, the first rooms and the title only (bot walks);
              loading screen stub in bank 13, emulator-tested only; cheats
              proved in the simulator on the 128K file: Infinite lives: the
              lives counter (63790) stayed 3 over 8 walks into the start
              room's fire (without it 2, 1, 0, game over); Immune to flame:
              the burn path (0xAFCD) never ran over 8 walks into the fire (6
              times without it); Immune to rat, dragon's fire, armorog, gator,
              sharp daggers: their rooms not reached; at each POKE site with
              the collision flag set the original goes on to its death code
              and the POKE takes the no-collision exit; dropped: Lives (asks
              the player for a value, which a patch cannot hold)

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
